   "subject": "Re: [camtrapR] Step to step guide for camtrapR",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n  \r\n    \r\n  \r\n  <div>\r\n    <p>Dear Letro, <br>\r\n    </p>\r\n    <p>there are four vignettes which explain the entire workflow. The\r\n      sample data these vignettes use are in the package, so you can\r\n      follow along. <br>\r\n    </p>\r\n    <p>You can find them on the <a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/camtrapR/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/camtrapR/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792460170149000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1iYyS2YCy9Fk85h5GBxL_m\">CRAN\r\n        page</a> (under Vignettes, they are numbered 1-4), on the <a href=\"https://jniedballa.github.io/camtrapR/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://jniedballa.github.io/camtrapR/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792460170149000&amp;usg=AOvVaw38z442FC6MYXNIxg3Remm5\">github page</a>\r\n      (under Articles), or directly within R(Studio):\r\n      ?`camtrapR-package`<br>\r\n    </p>\r\n    <p>Also, see the <a href=\"https://besjournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1111/2041-210X.12600\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://besjournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1111/2041-210X.12600&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792460170149000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0ypVcBAzdmB0g6hQuXEgGD\">original\r\n        publication</a> which explains the workflow (note it&#39;s a few\r\n      years old, and there are some new functions by now).</p>\r\n    <p>If you are new to R, I suggest to first get familiar with the\r\n      basics of R before using camtrapR, to avoid unnecessary\r\n      frustration. <br>\r\n    </p>\r\n    <p>Best regards,</p>\r\n    <p>Jürgen</p></div>"
    ],
